            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="DER01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Earl of Derby</roleName>
                        <forename>Edward</forename>
                        <surname>Stanley</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1752-09-12">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1834-10-21"/>
                    <occupation>sportsman</occupation>
                    <occupation>patron of horse-racing</occupation>
                    <occupation>occasional politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Edward Smith Stanley, twelfth earl of Derby (1752–1834) was a sportsman, patron
    of horse-racing, and an occasional politician and supporter of <persName key="FOX01">Charles James Fox</persName>. Godwin met with 
    him on several occasions, first at <persName key="LAU01">Lauderdale's</persName> and subsequently at <persName key="DEB01">Debrett's</persName>. Godwin noted the 
      death of the second countess of Derby on 23 April 1829 and the death of the Earl on 21 October 1834. </p>
                        <p>Godwin entered his name correctly under 1796 in the 1796 lists.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
